//! Carnatic music: swaras, melakartas, ragas, gamakas, talas and the
//! arithmetic of cadences.
//!
//! The model follows what the tradition writes down: the 16 swara names on
//! 12 positions; the 72 melakarta parent scales, generated by the same
//! combinatorial rule the Venkatamakhi scheme encodes; a raga as a
//! grammar over swaras (its ascent, descent, omitted notes and
//! characteristic phrases), not as a scale; ornaments (gamakas) as
//! continuous pitch curves; and talas as cycles of angas.
//!
//! Notation conventions vary between schools (swara numbering, akshara
//! counts, intonation of a swara in a given raga); where they do, the
//! choice made is stated where it is made.

pub mod gamaka;
pub mod korvai;
